DESCRIPTION >
    Wave-3 flexible_report Class-A dim-swap: group_by=ATTRIBUTION_STATUS. Clone of
    flexible_report_provider_by_site with the dim expr swapped to GROUP_COLUMNS.attribution_status
    (ATTRIBUTION_STATUS_SQL, attribution-engine.js:81) and the SAME external_event_id dedup carried
    from birth (#170). One row per attribution_status with the metric.

    MODEL-INDEPENDENT (verified): attribution_status is a CONVERSION-PROPERTY group_by —
    GROUP_COLUMNS.attribution_status = ATTRIBUTION_STATUS_SQL for all 4 touch models (first_touch/
    last_touch/first_touch_non_direct/last_touch_non_direct), and it references NO _nd touchpoint
    columns (only attribution_status/ingestion_method/stitching_method — all conversion props). For the
    *_non_direct models the live sql adds a _nd LEFT JOIN this dim never reads; it is 1:<=1 by
    distinct_id (non-fanning), so count()/SUM per attribution_status is identical whether or not it
    runs. WINDOW is a no-op (same reasoning as provider, proven GREEN on --live). So this ONE pipe
    serves group_by=attribution_status for all 4 touch models.

    dim = ATTRIBUTION_STATUS_SQL, typed-translated (§2.6): properties.attribution_status ->
    attribution_status (LowCardinality(Nullable(String)), events.datasource:35); properties.
    ingestion_method -> ingestion_method (LowCardinality(String), :32); properties.stitching_method ->
    stitching_method (LowCardinality(Nullable(String)), :34). EMPTY/NULL convention replicated exactly:
    COALESCE(NULLIF(attribution_status,''), multiIf(...)) — an empty/absent status falls through to the
    same multiIf fallback the HogQL uses, so buckets match. metric in {revenue, conversions} via the
    `metric` param. BASE-CASE GATE ONLY (no dim2/custom/filters, UTC, conversion_date); window-tolerant.
    Same params/output columns (dim_value, metric_value) so the wiring's positional remap is byte-identical.

    external_event_id DEDUP (identical to flexible_report_provider_by_site, #170): keep all
    null/empty-keyed rows; for a non-null key keep the GLOBAL-earliest-by-timestamp row (inner subquery
    NOT date-filtered, matching HogQL). Tie-break Tinybird event_id (HogQL uses uuid) — identical bucket
    for a genuine duplicate (it shares attribution_status+value). PARAM SHAPE: {{ String(site_id) }}
    referenced TWICE (outer + dedup subquery); date params once. MANDATORY before deploy:
    `tb --cloud deploy --check` (ST_Staging, NOT prod). VALUE-PARITY NOT RUN.

NODE flexible_report_attribution_status_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        COALESCE(NULLIF(attribution_status, ''), multiIf(ingestion_method = 'server_routed', 'attributed', stitching_method IS NOT NULL AND stitching_method != '' AND stitching_method != 'none', 'attributed', stitching_method = 'none', 'unattributed', 'unknown')) AS dim_value,
        {% if String(metric, 'conversions') == 'revenue' %}
        SUM(toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)))
        {% else %}
        count()
        {% end %} AS metric_value
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
      -- external_event_id dedup — carried from flexible_report_provider_by_site (#170), faithful port
      -- of the HogQL leg (attribution-engine.js:2397-2409). KEEP every null/empty-keyed row; for a
      -- non-null key keep the GLOBAL-earliest-by-timestamp row (inner subquery NOT date-filtered).
      -- Tie-break Tinybird event_id (HogQL uses uuid) — identical bucket for a genuine duplicate.
      AND (
        external_event_id IS NULL
        OR external_event_id = ''
        OR event_id IN (
          SELECT argMin(event_id, timestamp)
          FROM events
          WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
            AND event_type = '$conversion'
            AND external_event_id IS NOT NULL
            AND external_event_id != ''
          GROUP BY external_event_id
        )
      )
    GROUP BY dim_value
    ORDER BY metric_value DESC
    LIMIT 50000

TYPE endpoint
